│                                                                    │
│ This is the implementation of the _stream method in the            │
│ BedrockModel class. The method handles streaming conversations     │
│ with the Bedrock API. It formats the request, invokes the          │
│ streaming client method converse_stream, then iterates over the    │
│ streamed response chunks. It monitors these chunks and applies     │
│ some logic to determine if they contain guardrail data, if a tool  │
│ use event is occurring (using the has_tool_use flag), and if the   │
│ stop reason on a messageStop chunk needs to be overridden from     │
│ "end_turn" to "tool_use." It finally invokes a callback on each    │
│ processed chunk or event. It also contains error handling for AWS  │
│ client exceptions.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is specifically about the has_tool_use flag which is       │
│ currently only set to True on the presence of contentBlockStart    │
│ with toolUse in the chunk (if "contentBlockStart" in chunk and     │
│ chunk["contentBlockStart"].get("start", {}).get("toolUse"):). The  │
│ user reported that this fails in certain edge cases when toolUse   │
│ events appear instead as contentBlockDelta, causing the            │
│ stop_reason override logic to not trigger. This results in         │
│ premature ending of the agent loop by failing to override          │
│ "end_turn" to "tool_use."                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The intended behavior is for the stream processing loop to track   │
│ tool use events more comprehensively. It should set has_tool_use   │
│ to True not only when contentBlockStart with toolUse is            │
│ encountered but also when contentBlockDelta with toolUse is seen   │
│ in the streaming chunk. This would fix the edge cases where tool   │
│ use event start is represented by contentBlockDelta instead of     │
│ contentBlockStart. Consequently, the override logic should then    │
│ trigger correctly to change stopReason from "end_turn" to          │
│ "tool_use," allowing the agent loop to continue rather than        │
│ terminate. This preserves existing logic and error handling while  │
│ extending tracking robustness.                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ Plan for patch:                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Modify the condition that sets has_tool_use to include check    │
│    for contentBlockDelta with toolUse similar to contentBlockStart │
│    check.                                                          │
│  • Keep the existing logic for callback and stopReason override    │
│    unchanged except for this enhanced detection.                   │
